Description: KDE Plasma system tray menus for window tiling and screen resolution
 Two KDE Plasma 6 system tray widgets.
 .
 Window Tiling tiles the windows of the current desktop into columns, rows
 or a grid (automatically, or 2, 3 or 4 columns, 2 or 3 rows, a 2x2, 3x2 or
 4x2 grid), puts them back with Restore, can tile new windows as they open
 and snaps dropped windows into the column, row or grid cell under the
 pointer. The tiling runs in a KWin script.
 .
 Resolution Menu switches the screen resolution with kscreen-doctor from a
 list you edit, adding sizes the screen does not offer (KWin custom modes on
 Wayland, xrandr on X11).
 .
 Both widgets are put in each user's system tray at their next login, or
 right away by running plasma-tile-menu setup.
